{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (confirmed; fast path): docs/event-schema.md:51 statically enumerates six LINK relations and omits `caused_by`, while the same sentence explicitly cites `graph/_links.py:CANONICAL_RELATIONS`; src/rebar/graph/_links.py:17-34 contains seven canonical relations including `caused_by` and states it is directional, non-blocking, and never cycle-inducing. The closed design/implementation authority `isogonal-wedded-catfish` (0b96-cbcb-0ea2-479d) explicitly required docs/event-schema.md to document the seventh relation and defines those semantics; docs/ticket-model.md:148-160 and :189-194 already publish them. History discriminates the mechanism: commit 901241b218 added `caused_by` to code/help/ticket-model but did not modify docs/event-schema.md; later commit 693a6bf412 rewrote the LINK/UNLINK row and retained the six-value inventory. Therefore the changeable root cause is a stale manually duplicated inventory in docs/event-schema.md, not a runtime relation defect. Legitimacy: defect/incomplete implementation against the closed 0b96 design authority. Expected repair is docs-only semantics restoration plus a contract test tying the maintained event-schema LINK row to the canonical relation set; no caller behavior depends on the omission."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787091657072731001,"uuid":"7ddc5d0d-9d4b-4267-a59e-86961e64ddc9"}